  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Localized Multi-Hazard Anticipatory Action Facility Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1008000</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Pakistan, droughts, heat waves and floods occur regionally time and again. With anticipatory disaster relief, damage can be minimised, i.e. aid money is released if certain conditions are met - even before the disaster. Welthungerhilfe is creating the conditions in several regions with the &apos;START Network&apos;: This includes good local preparation, early warning systems and local experts who predict when, where and how a heat wave will develop, for example. Local organisations can then best help the people affected.</narrative>
  </description>
